y": "RumbleEmbed", "release_timestamp": 1778626861, "view_count": 11780, "like_count": 187, "dislike_count": 6, "description": "SIGN THE PETITION👇 End the 40 year reign of terror. Restore accountability and legal liability to vaccine manufacturers. www.vacsafety.org/petitionShow more This week on VSRF Live, we sit down with former Congresswoman Marjorie Taylor Greene for an unfiltered look inside Washington D.C. and why she chose to walk away.\nMs. Greene represented Georgia’s 14th congressional district from 2021 to 2026, serving three terms in Congress before resigning earlier this year. During her time in office, she became one of the most outspoken and combative voices in Congress, known for directly challenging party leadership, confronting entrenched interests, and taking positions few in Washington were willing to take.\nMs. Greene lays out what she calls the “Political Industrial Complex,” a system captured by donor money, powerful corporate lobbies, and entrenched interests, where major decisions are determined long before they ever reach a vote. From pharmaceutical influence to the liability protections surrounding vaccines, she explains why accountability is structurally blocked—and why even reform-minded leadership, including HHS Secretary Kennedy, runs into the same wall of pressure and constraint.\nIn this episode, Ms. Greene pulls back the curtain on Capitol Hill during the COVID era: mandates, restrictions, and the internal battles that followed her refusal to take the COVID vaccine or comply with masking rules. She details the steep financial penalties she faced, the pressure campaigns inside Congress, and what she witnessed behind closed doors, including repeated efforts to shut down meaningful investigation into vaccine safety.\nThe conversation also turns to the broader political landscape, including her break with Donald Trump and why attempts at reform from within the system continue to fail.\nMs. Greene closes with a clear warning and a call to action: change will not come from quietly waiting on elected officials to choose their constituents over their donors. Change comes when the American people unite across party lines and fight together. Make our voices heard. Apply relentless pressure. And never give up. Show less", "thumbnail": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/c0/s8/1/M/O/U/l/MOUlA.qR4e-small-VSRF-Live-227-Marjorie-Tayl..jpg", "display_id": "v77cobi", "fulltitle": "VSRF Live #227 - Marjorie Taylor Greene Inside Washington: What She Saw, Why She Left", "duration_string": "1:21:21", "upload_date": "20260507", "release_date": "20260512", "release_year": 2026, "is_live": false, "was_live": true, "epoch": 1794321271, "acodec": "aac", "vcodec": "none", "url": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/c0/s8/2/M/O/U/l/MOUlA.Gaa.rec.aac", "format_id": "audio-192p", "tbr": 191, "filesize": 117163991, "width": 0, "height": 192, "protocol": "https", "ext": "aac", "audio_ext": "aac", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 191, "resolution": "audio only", "aspect_ratio": 0.0, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate"}, "format": "audio-192p - audio only", "_type": "video", "_version": {"version": "2026.11.04.232659", "release_git_head": "412e7f0a4b0588fe884a02b344ac66a06538475b", "repository": "yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds"}}